.docname {Development}
.include {docs}

How to build, test and ship vCortex. To only **run** it, see [Usage](usage.qd).

## The tools

| For | Needs |
|---|---|
| Backend | A C++17 compiler, CMake 3.25+, Ninja, PCL, Eigen, nlohmann/json, Asio |
| Frontend | Node 22.18+ or 24.12+ |
| Docs | Quarkdown 2.7.0 |
| Containers | Docker or Podman |

PCL is the heavy one. On Fedora the packaged PCL pulls in VTK and Qt (about 2 GiB), so the
README builds the few PCL modules needed, once, into `~/.local/opt/pcl`. The backend's
`Dockerfile` does the same, with the same options.

## Build and run the backend

```sh
cd backend
cmake --preset dev              # Debug, Ninja, PCL from ~/.local/opt/pcl
cmake --build --preset dev
build/vcortex --port 9002
```

| Option | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `--port <n>` | Port for every route. Default 9002 |
| `--config <file>` | Start values for the model, for example `config/model.json` |
| `--map <file.pcd>` | Offline mode: open a saved map, accept no robot |

**Offline example.** `build/vcortex --map map.pcd --config config/model.json`. If a file
`trajectory.tum` sits next to `map.pcd`, it is read as the robot's path.

The preset also writes `build/compile_commands.json`, for editors that use clangd.

## What gets built

| Target | Holds | Needs |
|---|---|---|
| `vcortex_core` | domain, model, connectors, protocol | PCL, Eigen, nlohmann/json. No web server, no files |
| `vcortex_io` | server, store, worker, config, offline | `vcortex_core`, PCL's file reader, Crow, threads |
| `vcortex` | `main.cpp` | `vcortex_io` |
| `vcortex_tests` | the tests | `vcortex_core`, doctest |

The split is the same as the layers in [Folders](project-structure.qd). The tests link only
`vcortex_core`, so a test never touches the network or a file.

| Library | Version | Used for |
|---|---|---|
| PCL | 1.14+ (the images build 1.15.1) | Point cloud maths: dropping strays, floor plane, search |
| Eigen | any that PCL accepts | Vectors, boxes, rotations |
| nlohmann/json | 3.11+ | JSON in and out |
| Crow | 1.3.4, pinned by hash | HTTP and WebSocket server |
| doctest | 2.4.12, pinned by hash | Tests |

Crow is pinned to 1.3.4, which fixed a bypass of the login check in the WebSocket upgrade.
All warnings are on (`-Wall -Wextra -Wpedantic -Wshadow -Wconversion`) for our own code.

## Tests

```sh
cd backend
ctest --test-dir build          # or run build/vcortex_tests
```

**Real result on this machine:** 20 test cases, 54 checks, all passed.

| File | Cases | What it checks |
|---|---|---|
| `floor/free_space_test` | 4 | Doors split rooms; an aisle between desks does not |
| `wall/outline_test` | 1 | Each room has its own outline; a shared wall is in both |
| `wall/outline_steps_test` | 7 | L-shaped rooms, doors, furniture against a wall, corners |
| `wall/walls_test` | 2 | Two faces make one wall as thick as their distance; one face makes a default-thickness wall |
| `object/boxes_test` | 6 | A step, an L, a U, a ring: how many boxes each shape gives |

### Rooms drawn as text

A test draws its room in the file, and the helper turns the drawing into dots, as a lidar would.
One character is a 10 cm square.

| Character | Means |
|---|---|
| `.` | Floor seen |
| `#` | Wall: floor, low dots (10–30 cm) and tall dots (1.0 and 1.8 m) |
| `d` | Desk: floor, low dots and its top at 0.75 m; nothing tall |
| `P` | Floor, with a robot pose in the middle |
| (space) | Not seen |

**Example,** the real drawing of `a door between walls splits two rooms`: two rooms of
1.6 × 1.8 m, a wall between them, and a **0.9 m door** (the 9 rows with no `#` in the middle wall).
There is one pose `P` in each room.

```text
###################################
#................#................#
#................#................#
#................#................#
#................#................#
#................#................#
#.................................#
#.................................#
#.................................#
#.................................#
#........P................P.......#
#.................................#
#.................................#
#.................................#
#.................................#
#................#................#
#................#................#
#................#................#
#................#................#
###################################
```

The test checks that the model finds **2 rooms**, and that the squares under the two `P` belong
to different ones.

Each character becomes 4 × 4 dots, 2.5 cm apart, so each 5 cm square of the grid holds 2 × 2.
No square reads as unseen floor.

There are no tests yet for the server, the store, the worker, the connectors or the frontend.

## Build and run the frontend

See [Frontend](frontend.qd) for the commands. In short: `npm install`, then `npm run dev` for hot
reload; it sends `/api` and `/ws` to the backend on port 9002.

After a change to `backend/schema/twin.schema.json`, run `npm run generate-types`.

## Containers

.mermaid caption:{How the backend image is built. Only the last stage ships.}
    flowchart LR
        T[toolchain<br/>compiler, CMake, libs] --> P[pcl<br/>built from source, static]
        T --> C[crow<br/>source, checked by hash]
        P --> B[build<br/>one static program]
        C --> B
        B --> R[runtime<br/>distroless image]

| Image | Base | Holds |
|---|---|---|
| `vcortex-backend` | `distroless/static-debian13:nonroot` | One static program, plus `config/` |
| `vcortex-frontend` | the same | The Caddy program and the built page |

- **Distroless** means the image has no shell and no tools. There is little to attack.
- PCL is built from source, static, and without VTK and Qt: the image stays small.
- The program is linked as `-static-pie`: one file, with address randomisation kept.
- The last build stage runs **offline**: Crow's source comes from an earlier stage, and tests
  are off (`BUILD_TESTING=OFF`).

### `compose.yaml`

| Service | Port | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `backend` | 9002 | The robot's bridge connects to `/ingest` here. `./data` is mounted read-only at `/data` |
| `frontend` | 8081 (8080 inside) | Open this in the browser |

Both run with a **read-only file system**, **no Linux capabilities**, `no-new-privileges` and
`restart: unless-stopped`. The token comes from `.env` (copy `.env.example`):
`VCORTEX_INGEST_TOKEN`. Empty means no check.

```sh
cp .env.example .env
docker compose up --build       # or: podman compose up --build
```

## The documentation

```sh
cd docs
quarkdown c main.qd -o output   # the output folder is not in git
```

| Job | When | Does |
|---|---|---|
| `build` | A push to `main`, or a pull request, that touches `docs/` | Builds the HTML |
| `deploy` | A push to `main` only | Publishes it on GitHub Pages |

Every action in the workflow is pinned to a **full commit hash**, with the version in a comment.
A tag can be moved; a hash cannot.

## Gaps found

| What | Where |
|---|---|
| The only workflow builds the docs. Nothing builds or tests the backend or the frontend on a push | `.github/workflows/` |
| `compose.yaml` has a stale TODO about `--map`. To use offline mode in a container, edit its `command` line by hand | `compose.yaml` |
| No tests for `io/`, `connectors/`, `protocol/` and the frontend | `backend/tests/`, `frontend/` |
